  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 206 AM EDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nOverall upper level pattern is transitioning to a longwave\ntrough which will settle in for the next several days. A series\nof waves will pass through with timing and strength differences\ncausing challenges on precip chances into at least Thursday\nnight. A weak cold front extended from northern Lower MI to\neastern IA. This feature will edge ever so slowly east with each\nimpulse and a modest LLJ allowing for areas of storms to \ndevelop and move N and E. The current area of showers and storms\nwill attempt to edge east over the next several hours, but \nshould weaken as it outruns the 20 to 30 kt LLJ as well as \nbetter forcing. A somewhat stronger trough will intersect the \nfrontal boundary, allowing for a strengthening LLJ with \nredevelopment of convection expected during the day over eastern\nIA. The LLJ and eastern movement of the trough will allow some \nchance for this precip to make it into far W/NW areas late this \nafternoon and moreso this evening but it will fight to make it \nvery far east as the front slows further. Have attempted to slow\narrival this afternoon and focus highest (likely) pops in W/NW \nareas this evening before the overall area likely weakens. \nThereafter running with slgt chc to chc pops given the front \nslowly edging into the CWA and stalling/washing out with time. \nModels vary on degree of potential redevelopment during the day \nThursday, but with plenty of moisture and limited CAPE at least \nmid to high chc pops warranted with possibility for higher pops\nneeded depending on overnight convection impacts. High PWATs \nwill bring a threat for heavy rainfall with the greatest \nconcerns existing where repeated convection occurs. \n\nNo sig changes beyond Thurs given challenges for overall timing\nand impacts from additional waves as the upper level trough\nremains in place into early next week. The main focus for\ngreater heat will remain over the 4 Corners area through the\nweekend with a somewhat more zonal flow beginning to set up next\nweek which may allow some of this to move in.",
